{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/366","id":4718929602,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGUUmwg","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/366","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/366.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/366.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/366","number":366,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[2303016] Credited direct capacity proof (already solved, 1/5)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Accepted outcome\n\n2303016 / AMR-022-3016, Hayman–Lingham Problem 3.16: **already_solved, 1/5**, retained as a credited direct-proof reconstruction and partial research outcome. No novelty or first-priority claim.\n\nFor compact E in R^n, n>=3, the points x in E with finite integral_0^1 cap(E intersect closed B(x,r))/r^(n-1) dr form a polar set. The source already knows this consequence of Kellogg and asks for a direct proof. The packet supplies an explicit Newtonian energy proof, crediting the earlier compact-localization/capacitary-measure strategy of Hedberg–Wolff (1983), pp.173–174.\n\n## Proof and exact scope\n\nThe proof establishes equilibrium first variation and a global weak potential bound, proves Borel measurability, selects a positive-capacity compact set with uniformly small tails and diameter, and obtains the contradiction by extended-valued layer cake. It assumes ordinary Borel Choquet capacitability and capacity-zero/polar equivalence; it avoids the fine-topological Choquet property, Kellogg, Dirichlet irregularity, Wiener equivalence, and a silent Bessel/Newtonian kernel substitution.\n\nSharpness is limited to positive decreases in the denominator exponent, nonnegative weights integrable against dr/r, and an uncountable polar segment example. Arbitrary nonintegrable gauges and exhaustive historical priority remain outside the proved scope. The editors' no-progress update and historical duplicate-search narrative are not priority certificates.\n\n## Validation and disposition\n\nThree new primary-first independent mathematical reviews found no mandatory defect. Root reviewed the complete proof and every executed checker. All 2,690 author and 1,909 historical controls reproduce byte-exact; separate new controls supplement the analytical proof and do not establish polarity by sampling. Root verified all 22 original Git/API/disk files, the actual 14-file one-turn checkpoint, all 48 nested manifest bindings, both closed approach reviews, and every captured approach-review command. Final literal live-head and actual integration checks are recorded in the dedicated descending audit.\n\nAll 21 original mathematical/review files are retained unchanged. The refreshed PR changes only its target folder and its own QUEUE status/turn cells against current main. Accept as credited partial findings, without a paper, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker row, or GitHub release.\n","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:35:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T17:52:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,